      "Corporate Income Tax (CIT): Companies registered in Sri Lanka pay income tax on their taxable profits. The standard rate is 30%, with a lower rate of 14% applying to qualifying small and medium enterprises and certain priority sectors. Annual returns are due by November 30.",
      "Value Added Tax (VAT): Businesses with annual turnover exceeding the VAT registration threshold must register for VAT and file periodic returns. The standard rate is 18%. VAT on inputs (what you pay to suppliers) is offset against VAT on outputs (what you charge customers).",
      "Social Security Contribution Levy (SSCL): This levy applies to businesses above a specified turnover threshold. It is calculated on turnover and filed quarterly.",
      "Withholding Tax (WHT) and Advance Income Tax (AIT): Certain payments—professional fees, rent, dividends—require the payer to withhold a percentage and remit it to the IRD on behalf of the recipient.",
      "Statement of Estimated Tax (SET): Companies must file quarterly estimated tax installments based on the current year's anticipated liability. Underpayment results in interest charges.",
      "SMART Pvt Ltd's tax team in Trincomalee handles all these obligations for businesses across Sri Lanka. Contact us to ensure your tax compliance is current and accurate."
